{"title":"Career Roadmap · ICU Technologist","role":"ICU Technologist","summary":"An ICU Technologist is an allied-health professional who supports multidisciplinary critical-care teams in the management of critically ill patients. With a Respiratory Care Technology background, the strongest positioning is around respiratory support, mechanical ventilation, airway equipment, patient monitoring, respiratory procedures and ICU equipment management.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Respiratory Care Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An ICU Technologist is an allied-health professional who supports multidisciplinary critical-care teams in the management of critically ill patients. With a Respiratory Care Technology background, the strongest positioning is around respiratory support, mechanical ventilation, airway equipment, patient monitoring, respiratory procedures and ICU equipment management."},{"type":"p","text":"The role requires knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Critical-care physiology"},{"text":"Respiratory physiology"},{"text":"Mechanical ventilation"},{"text":"Airway management"},{"text":"Patient monitoring"},{"text":"ABG interpretation"},{"text":"Oxygen therapy"},{"text":"Infection control"},{"text":"Emergency response"},{"text":"ICU equipment"},{"text":"Respiratory therapy"},{"text":"Clinical documentation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A realistic pathway is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Respiratory Care Technology Degree","Respiratory / ICU Clinical Training","Respiratory Care Technologist","ICU Technologist","Senior ICU Technologist","Critical-Care Technologist / Lead","ICU Operations / Clinical Coordinator"]},{"type":"note","label":"Professional note","text":"Exact titles and scope of practice vary by hospital and applicable professional requirements. Diagnosis, prescribing and medical decisions remain the responsibility of appropriately qualified clinicians."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Stage","Typical Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Anatomy, physiology and respiratory foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Respiratory care + critical-care technology"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Mechanical ventilation + ICU practice"}],[{"text":"Clinical internship"},{"text":"ICU/respiratory clinical exposure"}],[{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Respiratory Care / ICU Technologist"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"Experienced ICU Technologist"}],[{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Senior / Lead ICU Technologist"}],[{"text":"8–12 years"},{"text":"Critical-Care Coordinator"}],[{"text":"12+ years"},{"text":"ICU Operations / Clinical Technology Management"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year 1 — Biomedical & Respiratory Foundation","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human anatomy"},{"text":"Physiology"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Pathology"},{"text":"Pharmacology fundamentals"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"Patient care"},{"text":"Infection control"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Respiratory sciences"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Upper and lower respiratory tract"},{"text":"Lung anatomy"},{"text":"Alveoli"},{"text":"Pulmonary circulation"},{"text":"Ventilation"},{"text":"Perfusion"},{"text":"Gas exchange"},{"text":"Oxygen transport"},{"text":"Carbon-dioxide transport"},{"text":"Acid-base balance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cardiovascular foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cardiac output"},{"text":"Blood pressure"},{"text":"Perfusion"},{"text":"Cardiac-respiratory interaction"},{"text":"Oxygen delivery"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 objective"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a strong foundation in re